Local patch for 3rd/cproc, applied to the build copy by scripts/setup-qbe.sh after cproc-empty-struct.patch.

Copying a zero-size struct (EDG's empty C++ classes: lambda closures, comparators, allocators passed by value)
emitted one `loadub`/`storeb` pair, because funccopy() copies at least one unit. The store went to a zero-byte
slot, which QBE places at the frame pointer, so it overwrote the low byte of the saved %rbp: the caller then
ran with a corrupted frame pointer after the callee returned (found with nlohmann::json: std::all_of(first,
last, lambda) took the closure by value; `mov %al,0x0(%rbp)` in the generated all_of). A zero-size copy now
emits nothing. Test: tests/cases/qbe_empty_struct_copy.cpp.
--- a/qbe.c
+++ b/qbe.c
@@ -429,6 +429,10 @@
 	unsigned long long off;

 	assert((align & align - 1) == 0);
+	/* an empty struct or union (size 0, see cproc-empty-struct.patch) has nothing to copy; the loop
+	 * below always runs once and would write one byte past the zero-size destination */
+	if (size == 0)
+		return;
 	class = 'w';
 	switch (align) {
 	case 1: load = ILOADUB, store = ISTOREB; break;
